<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · concept</p><h1 class="enc-title">Repatriation of cultural property</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as repatriation, restitution</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Repatriation of cultural property refers to the return of artworks and artefacts removed from their countries or communities of origin, often through conquest or colonial looting. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benin-bronzes">Benin Bronzes</a>, some 3,000 works taken by British forces from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benin-empire">Benin Empire</a> in 1897, are the central case in the global debate. Nigerian and Edo demands for their return have led several museums to restitute objects.</p></div>
